3. According to the judgment of the researcher, it is suitable for enrollment;
4. Can walk independently without assistance;
5. The subjects voluntarily joined this study and signed an informed consent form, with good compliance and cooperation in follow-up.

Exclusion Criteria:

1. Pregnant or lactating women;
2. Severe active infection
3. Unable to walk
4. Cannot be active (more than two days)
5. Severe neurological or cardiac damage
6. Severe respiratory insufficiency
7. Uncontrollable pain
8. Those who have perceptual barriers or cognitive and Communication disorder and are unable to cooperate;
9. Participated in other sports groups during the research period;
10. According to the judgment of the researchers, the subjects may have other factors that may lead to the forced termination of this study, such as other serious illnesses (including mental illness) requiring concurrent treatment, serious laboratory test abnormalities, accompanied by family or social factors, which may affect the safety of the subjects, or the collection of data and samples;

