详细说明:
This pilot study will take place in the Mobile Healthcare Unit (motorized vehicle) that will travel to 10 Indigenous and/or remote communities.This study aims at collecting cardiovascular (CV) data and delivering culturally appropriate research and care in underserved/underrepresented populations. Collaborating members of the communities visited will be involve in the mobile care service and will assist as translators. Recruitment and data collection will be carried out by the investigator at the IUCPQ-ULaval in collaboration with the participating communities. This study was co-designed and accepted by health departments and participating communities. Each participant will undergo a comprehensive assessment of CV risk factors and CV conditions at the beginning of the study. This assessment will be standardized and will include the following elements:

* Clinical examination including anthropometric measurements;
* Auscultation by a cardiologist with a digital stethoscope;
* Translated and validated questionnaires on demographics and medical history;
* Pregnancy and reproductive health questionnaires;
* Blood pressure, assessed by oscillometry;
* Peripheral artery disease assessment;
* Cardiometabolic blood markers (NT-proBNP, HbA1C, hs-CRP, CBC, lipids, etc.)
* Arrythmia and atrial fibrillation, assessed by electrocardiogram;
* Anthropometric indices and body fat distribution by elastography;
* Maximal stress test on a treadmill;
* Questionnaire on participant satisfaction and areas of improvement in health equity.

