主要终点:
Desirability of Outcome Ranking (DOOR) at Day 70

Composite ordinal outcome adapted for Gram-positive cardiac infections. Participants will be ranked from most to least desirable outcome as follows:

1. = alive with no clinical failure, infectious complication, or serious adverse event/adverse event leading to study drug discontinuation;
2. = alive with 1 of these events;
3. = alive with 2 of these events;
4. = alive with all 3 of these events;
5. = death. Within each rank, ties will be resolved using net change in EQ-5D score from baseline to Day 70, with greater improvement indicating a more desirable outcome.

Day 70 post-enrolment

